From 432e37e6cc5d4b9d77510f54bc28945f0830b6db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:00:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][GBM] Expert settings: the form of the Dolby Vision
 metadata, as Hades sends it or as set-top boxes do

The choices of the form of the metadata and of the AVI InfoFrame, in the
"Dolby Vision engine" group (expert level), read when native output starts.
Each default is what Hades 1.1 sends, which follows the TV's own player
playing the file (the whole RPU to the TV's display management, the level 5
block and the trims with it); the other values are what licensed set-top
boxes send (Dolby's IDK 2.6 on an Amlogic player; the OPPO UDP-203 as
fandangos read it), which simplify the metadata on their way to the TV. They
are for a comparison on a display, and for a display where a user finds one
better:

- videoscreen.hadesdvl5form, the active area (level 5): Hades' own (the
  default), Hades' own without one made where the video has none (as the TV's
  own player for an encode without one), as in the video, or not sent (as
  licensed set-top boxes);
- videoscreen.hadesdvlevelorder, the blocks in the order of their level, as
  set-top boxes send them: off (the order of the video);
- videoscreen.hadesdvl254zero, level 254 with version 0: off;
- videoscreen.hadesdvl3neutral, a neutral level 3 for content mapping v2.9: off;
- videoscreen.hadesdvavibt2020, BT.2020 in the AVI InfoFrame: off.

Strings in English (core 62350-62363) and Spanish (Estuary 54370-54383, es_es,
es_ar, es_mx); the log line of the engine says the form.
---
